# Runtime data — never commit citizen uploads or model weights.
#
# Every path here is ANCHORED with a leading slash. An unanchored `models/`
# matches at any depth, and it silently excluded the entire `backend/nemesis/db/
# models/` ORM package — the §9.2 schema would have been absent from the commit
# with no error anywhere, because `git add` reports nothing for an ignored path.
# Model weights actually live in the `modelcache` Docker volume mounted at
# /models, so these rules only ever needed to cover a repo-local override of
# NEMESIS_MODEL_CACHE_DIR.
/data/
/uploads/
/models/
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.onnx

# Validation artefacts are regenerated, not committed — but anchored for the
# same reason, so a committed measurement that backs a decision (for example
# docs/reports/hnsw-recall.json, cited by ADR-0012) is not swept up with them.
/reports/*.json
!reports/.gitkeep
